// EDITION: rust
// The rust edition's standard library (0.27): the API of the std that
// rust-edition programs use from 0.27.2 on, and that `fix --edition rust`
// (0.27.3) rewrites MVS programs against. In 0.27.0 it was a spec: every
// item's signature in its final form and its doc, the bodies to come;
// 0.27.2 writes them, Rust's. It is checked as its own root,
// `volec check --edition rust compiler/std2/std.vl`; rust-edition
// programs still run on MVS's std through ed270's reference-typed
// signatures until 0.27.2 builds this tree into the compiler
// (compiler/std/embed.sh --edition rust).
//
// It is a redesign, not a port of compiler/std (docs/design/rust-surface-plan.md,
// §2, §3, §6):
// - `v.get(i)` is `Option<&T>`, iterators yield `&T` and `iter_mut` `&mut T`;
//   maps have `entry`, and `Option` has `take`, `as_ref` and `as_mut`;
// - allocation is a capability: there is no default allocator, a
//   container names its allocator type `A`, every allocation outside a
//   container's own operations takes an allocator value, last (`_in`), and
//   `Clone` reuses the stored allocator while `clone_in(a)` moves to another;
// - every iterator has a named type: std needs no `impl Trait` in return
//   position;
// - std's paths are Rust's (std::vec::Vec, std::collections::HashMap,
//   std::alloc::Arena), and the prelude is Rust's with vole's additions.
//
// Each item's line in compiler/std2/checklist.tsv (tools/std2-checklist.py)
// says whether it is kept from MVS's std, renamed, changed or new, which
// MVS items are gone and into what, the features it needs, and the
// gate-1 test that covers it. Markers in an item's comment feed it:
// `// later: NAME` (a feature the rust front reports as
// `edition.later: NAME (0.27.N)`), `// mvs: PATH` (the MVS item it
// replaces, when its name or place differs), `// std2: renamed` and
// `// std2: changed: WHY`.
//
// Two kinds of item are the compiler's, as MVS's are: an item over
// `[T; N]` for every N, `#[array_builtin(N)]` (until const generics), and
// a trait's impls for the primitive types, `#[builtin_impls(i8, ...,
// bool)]` on the trait (each type listed gets `impl Trait for P`; char's
// come with the char feature). Both wait for 0.27.2 (array_builtin,
// primitive_builtin), and the checklist gives each trait's builtin impls
// a line.

